gain restored the preview with identical content (Ada Lovelace ... About Me ... Career History) and the Modern template rendering; editor fields unchanged.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Card menu > Duplicate created \\\"Data Scientist Resume (Copy)\\\" with all content copied; renamed the copy to \\\"ML Engineer Application\\\" via the rename dialog; edited the copy (name Ada L. Byron, email ada.copy@example.com, company CopyCorp AI) and the source \\\"Data Scientist Resume\\\" still showed Ada Lovelace / ada@example.com / Difference Ltd.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Dashboard holds 6 distinct resumes in the session: 3 seeded plus \\\"Data Scientist Resume\\\" (created + fully edited), \\\"ML Engineer Application\\\" (duplicated + renamed + independently edited) and \\\"Temp Delete Me\\\" (created). Each opens with its own content and can be renamed/duplicated/deleted from its card menu.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Search \\\"rEsUmE\\\" returned the 4 titles containing \\\"resume\\\" (case-insensitive); \\\"designer\\\" returned only Product Designer Resume; clearing the box restored all 6. Sort \\\"Oldest First\\\" listed Software Engineer (Jan 2024) → Marketing Manager → Product Designer → Data Scientist → ML Engineer → Temp Delete Me, and \\\"Newest First\\\" gave the exact reverse order.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No creation-date filter exists on the dashboard\", \"actual\": \"Dashboard offers only a title search box and a sort select (Newest/Oldest/Title A-Z/Z-A). There are no date inputs anywhere on the page (querySelectorAll for input[type=date|month|datetime-local] returns none; the only input is \\\"Search resumes...\\\"), so an exact creation date or date range cannot be applied or cleared. Typing a date (\\\"Feb 25, 2024\\\") into the search box returns 0 results.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-9\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No date-period validation for work or education entries\", \"actual\": \"Experience: start=2030-05 (future) with end=2019-01 (before start) accepted silently, preview showed \\\"May 2030 - Jan 2019\\\". Education: start=2018-09 with end=2017-01 accepted silently, preview showed \\\"Sep 2018 - Jan 2017\\\". No error message, field highlight, or toast in either case.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Both experience and education dates use input[type=month] and render as \\\"Mon YYYY\\\" (e.g. \\\"Jan 2020 - Jun 2022\\\", \\\"Sep 2014 - Jun 2018\\\"). Checking \\\"I currently work here\\\" on an entry with end=2022-06 cleared the value to \\\"\\\" and set the end-date input disabled=true; preview showed \\\"Jan 2020 - Present\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Resume data is not persisted across a page reload\", \"actual\": \"Before reload the dashboard had 5 resumes (3 seeded + created \\\"Data Scientist Resume\\\" with full edits + duplicated/renamed \\\"ML Engineer Application\\\"; \\\"Temp Delete Me\\\" deleted). After reloading http://localhost:7005/ only the 3 seeded resumes (Product Designer, Marketing Manager, Software Engineer) remain — the created, edited, duplicated and renamed versions were all lost.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Dashboard rename dialog accepts a whitespace-only title, wiping the resume title; editor rename reverts silently with no feedback\", \"actual\": \"Dashboard card menu > Rename: entering \\\"   \\\" and clicking Save closed the dialog and set the card title to an empty string (dashboard.resumes.item.n6c2auer8jq name = \\\"\\\"), with no validation message. Editor title rename with \\\"   \\\" or \\\"\\\" reverted to the previous title but showed no toast/inline error either.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Typing contact fields, summary, experience/education entries and skills updated preview.* observables instantly with no save action; selecting Classic/Minimal/Modern templates re-rendered the preview immediately. No manual save control exists and no refresh was needed.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Moving Skills above Education and toggling Education visibility off/on changed the preview instantly (headings order About Me/Career History/Core Skills/Academics; Education content removed then restored). After navigating to the dashboard and reopening the resume, the custom order (Skills before Education) and visibility state were preserved.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"No save button exists; all edits auto-persisted. Moving between Contact/Summary/Experience/Education/Skills/Template/Sections tabs kept edits; returning to dashboard showed card \\\"Data Scientist Resume - Updated Aug 27, 2026\\\" (today's date, reflecting the update) and reopening restored all content unchanged.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"With long summary + long descriptions (preview text ~1824 chars), the Modern preview rendered all visible sections with content (contact, About Me, Career History, Core Skills, Academics). The preview column grows with content (no fixed-height clipping) and the page scrolls (scrollHeight 1316 > viewport 720); after scrolling to the bottom the last preview element (education dates \\\"Sep 2014 - Jun 2018\\\") was fully inside the viewport.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After switching among all